{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792761892,"nonce":"1Ghr+jK4IihVIP2/X2XXBpWP6aY=","title":"Persist Git author avatars and retain successful images on lookup failure","message":"Author avatars currently live only in a repository-scoped memory cache. Restarting loses successful downloads, switching repositories repeats lookups for the same author, and an expired successful entry can be replaced by a temporary failure. Add bounded compressed-image disk persistence on the profile worker, provider/author identity sharing, and failure fallback to the last successful image. Keep decoded textures view-owned and preserve capability checks and cancellation. Verify offline process restart, repository changes, failed refreshes, cache bounds and owner cleanup.","files":null}]}